 # Scene Representation and Partitioning
 
-Also called: Spatial Partitioning, Scene Decomposition, Block-based Representation
 
 ## Overview
-This family of methods addresses the scalability limits of single-network NeRFs by decomposing the scene into multiple, smaller representations (submodules, blocks, or fields) that are optimized and queried independently [S1]. While the parent [Scene Representation and Architecture](11368-scene-representation-and-architecture.md) establishes the global mapping from 6D coordinates to radiance properties, these methods partition the domain to enable parallel training, reduce memory footprint, or handle dynamic content [G]. They differ from siblings like [Specific Model Architectures](8585-specific-model-architectures.md) by focusing on the structural decomposition of the scene space rather than the internal topology of the neural network itself [G].
